cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ProChoice: Composite LLM and Coding Agent Harness Pareto Leaderboards"
message: "If you use ProChoice rankings, methodology, or compiled benchmark snapshots in research or evaluations, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Retrograde Labs"
    website: "https://inretrograde.io"
repository-code: "https://github.com/RetrogradeLabs/pro-choice"
url: "https://prochoice.industries"
license: MIT
version: "3.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-22"
abstract: "ProChoice aggregates 47 strictly private held-out and live blind-arena LLM and coding agent benchmarks across 15 daily sources into six cost-quality composite indices covering Coding, Writing, Design, Research, Cyber, and Harnesses using provider-balanced anchor standardization, empirical reliability, discrimination, anchor-breadth, and additive Kish redundancy weights, measurement-only heteroscedastic REML Empirical Bayes denoising, active-set monotone effort cost regression, and bootstrap Pareto frontier analysis."
keywords:
  - llm-leaderboard
  - llm-benchmarks
  - ai-evaluation
  - coding-agents
  - pareto-frontier
  - psychometrics
  - empirical-bayes
  - open-data
